        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Eugène Ionesco, Paul Scott\n- Works: Amédée, or How to Get Rid of It, Oriflamme, The Raj Quartet\n- Roles: playwright, novelist, poet\n- Topics: French Avant-garde theatre\n\nFacts:\n- Eugène Ionesco was born as Eugen Ionescu on 26 November 1909 and died on 28 March 1994.\n- Eugène Ionesco was a Romanian-French playwright who wrote mostly in French and became one of the foremost figures of French Avant-garde theatre.\n- Paul Mark Scott was born on 25 March 1920 and died in March 1978.\n- Paul Scott was an English novelist, playwright, and poet best known for The Raj Quartet.\n- Amédée, or How to Get Rid of It is a 1954 play by Eugène Ionesco.\n- Amédée, or How to Get Rid of It was based on Eugène Ionesco's earlier short story Oriflamme.",
